{"Backup codes consumption leaves null entries in codes array by setting backupCodes[index] = null, which will cause UI breakage when formatBackupCode receives null": 0.6371357440948486, "Missing imports for React/Hooks in TwoFactor component - useState and useFormContext are used but not imported, causing compile/runtime errors": 0.09368854016065598, "Disable-2FA API path with backup code does not actually disable 2FA - it validates the backup code but does not update the user record to clear backupCodes or twoFactorEnabled": 0.09814392030239105, "Missing encryption key (CALENDSO_ENCRYPTION_KEY) causes server error without fallback handling, leading to server instability in misconfigured environments": 0.2633245885372162, "No end-to-end Playwright test covers signing in using a backup code after 2FA is required": 0.6600303053855896, "AES algorithm name 'aes256' in crypto module may be invalid - Node.js expects named cipher like 'aes-256-cbc' or 'aes-256-ctr'": 0.017447911202907562, "EnableTwoFactorModal.tsx renders backupCodes array without filtering out nulls, causing formatBackupCode to fail or display 'null'": 0.17721784114837646, "DisableTwoFactorModal calls TwoFactorAuthAPI.disable with only two arguments (password, totpCode) but API expects three parameters including backupCode": 0.01049919705837965, "Backup codes are exposed in API response during TOTP setup - potential leakage beyond onboarding step": 0.2499447464942932, "Existing users with 2FA enabled but no backup codes will have null backupCodes, but code paths assume an encrypted string when decrypting": 0.5915831923484802, "Potential duplication of UI logic across BackupCode.tsx, EnableTwoFactorModal backup codes screen, and login Lost Access backup codes": 0.00830460712313652, "No explicit UI path to reset or display fresh state after disabling 2FA when backupCodes are cleared to null": 0.004357695579528809, "New i18n keys for backup codes added to English locale but may need analogous updates in other locales": 0.06487830728292465}